-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",357,{
[11393]="70046BF9\n1\tDefeat spiders and destroy spider-webs\t\n2\tDestroy spider-webs in Thurindath (total: 8)\030Defeat spiders in Thurindath (total: 8)\tSpiders and their webs can be found within the old Ranger refuge of Thurindath in south-eastern North Ithilien. You have discovered the refuge of Thurindath overrun with great spiders and their webs. You should defeat them and clear the refuge of their webbing.\n3\tTalk to Mablung at Henneth Annûn\tMablung can be found at Henneth Annûn. You have cleared the old Ranger refuge of Thurindath of spiders and their webs, but you should inform the Rangers of what you discovered.\n",
[11394]="7000AE1E\n1\tDeliver the sinew to Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith\030Collect drake-sinew (total: 5)\tDrakes can be found in Arador's End, north of Tol Ascarnen. Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith has asked you to assist her in crafting a horn to call forces to fight against Angmar's army when they assail Tol Ascarnen. To do this, she asks that you collect sinews from the drakes of Arador's End with which to bind the Horn of Tol Ascarnen. She suggests you take allies.\n",
[11395]="7000B0E3\n1\tBring the strawberry dessert-wine to Baldwin Foxtail\030Collect strawberry dessert-wine (total: 5)\tBaldwin Foxtail is at the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire. Baldwin Foxtail has asked you to bring him five bottles of strawberry dessert-wine for the cooks of the Mathom Society.\n",
[11396]="70058578\n1\tConfront the raiding party of the Drekvath River\tThe path across the Drekvath River can be found east of Shakal-atrâd. You should confront the raiding party of the Drekvath River.\n2\tTalk to Yrsa Spearwife on the road\tThe Drekvath River can be found east of Shakal-atrâd. You should talk to Yrsa Spearwife by the Drekvath River.\n3\tTalk to Yrsa Spearwife at Shakal-atrâd\tYrsa Spearwife can be found at Shakal-atrâd. You should talk to Yrsa Spearwife at Shakal-atrâd.\n4\tShakal-atrâd can be found in Elderslade. You should give Beorining-made spears to the dwarves at Shakal-atrâd.\t\n5\tAssist Thyra at Shakal-atrâd\030Assist Sighild at Shakal-atrâd\030Assist Hertha at Shakal-atrâd\tThyra, Sighild, and Hertha can all be found at Shakal-atrâd. You should assist the Beornings at Shakal-atrâd.\n6\tFind and aid Skarding Wargsbane\tSkarding Wargsbane can be found somewhere on the battlefield. You should find and aid Skarding Wargsbane.\n7\tAssist Langhár at Zarkul-sulûn\030Assist Varthmath at Zarkul-sulûn\tLanghár and Varthmath can be found at Zarkul-sulûn. You should assist Langhár and Varthmath.\n8\tTalk to Langhár at Zarkul-sulûn\tLanghár can be found at Zarkul-sulûn. You should talk to Langhár.\n",
[11397]="7006B9D0\n1\tSpeak with Agazi near the rockslide to the west\tSpeak with Agazi near the rockslide on the road to Ambarûl to the west.\n2\tDefeat spiny lizards (total: 8)\tDefeat spiny lizards near the rockslide blocking the path to Ambarûl.\n3\tReturn to Agazi\tReturn to Agazi near the rockslide blocking the path to Ambarûl in the west.\n4\tSpeak with Balgiba in the Channel of Bâdizal\tSpeak with Balgiba near the Channel of Bâdizal to the south of Maurûsh.\n5\tCollect tortoise shells (total: 5)\tBalgiba has asked you to gather tortoise shells for him near the Channel of Bâdizal for the armour he is trying to craft.\n6\tReturn to Balgiba with the tortoise shells\tBring the tortoise shells back to Balgiba in the Channel of Bâdizal.\n7\tReturn to Galâmka in Ub Nishir\tReturn to Galâmka in Maurûsh and update him on Agazi and Balgiba.\n",
[11398]="70002CD2\n1\tDestroy catapults (total: 2)\030Destroy siege-towers (total: 2)\tThe war-engines -- siege towers and catapults -- of the Angmarim are in the eastern part of Ram Dúath. Tuokki has asked you to help destroy the Angmarim siege-towers and catapults.\n2\tTalk to Chief Tuokki\tChief Tuokki is at the Suuri-lehmä camp in Ram Dúath. You should return to Tuokki with word of your success.\n",
[11399]="70017590\n1\tGive the items to Frosti Groundshaker in Thorin's Hall\tFrosti Groundshaker is in Thorin's Hall, by the auctioneers south of the throne. You should take the pieces to Frosti Groundshaker in Thorin's Hall so that he may shed some light upon what may be going on.\n2\tReturn to Armbeald in the Redhorn Lodes\tArmbeald is at the Orc-Watch in the Redhorn Lodes of Moria. Frosti Groundshaker has made you an effigy with some runes that may help to draw the attention of the Orc-wraith. You should return to Armbeald in Moria and he will instruct you on what to do next.\n",
[11400]="70046896\n1\tYou should bring the armour to the soldiers in and around Aragorn's Pavilion, on the after-battle Pelennor.\t\n2\tTalk to Angbor\tYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n",
[11401]="7001B702\n1\tClaim the lower courtyard\tThe doors of Dannenglor have been sealed. To infiltrate the ancient ruins, you will have to enter through the lower courtyard and work your way up.\n2\tClaim the south entranceway\030Claim the west bridge\030Claim the east terrace\tThe heart of Dannenglor is a large open courtyard with a southern gate, western bridge, and eastern terrace. All three of those will need to be in your control to advance.\n3\tOpen the upper courtyard\tThe small upper courtyard is the only thing keeping you from the sorcerer.\n4\tDefeat the sorcerer and claim the sorcerer's chamber\tTo take Dannenglor for the Golden Host and free its prisoners, the sorcerer residing here must be defeated and his chamber claimed.\n",
[11402]="70029FC2\n1\tComplete 'Strike Against Dannenglor' in a raid group\tSeveral Elves and Rangers have been taken prisoner by a sorcerer within the ancient Elf-ruins of Dannenglor.\n",
[11403]="700276EE\n1\tDefeat Dunlending raiders (total: 6)\030Defeat Dunlending looters (total: 4)\tThe Dunlending raiders were last seen scattering into the hills west of the Ford of Isen. The Rohirrim quartermaster asked you to hunt down the Dunlending raiders who attacked the encampment and chase them from the area.\n2\tTalk to the Rohirrim quartermaster\tThe Rohirrim quartermaster is at the Ford of Isen. You should return to the Rohirrim quartermaster and tell him that the Dunlending raiders have been driven off.\n",
[11404]="70028C92\n1\tTalk to Answith in the Isendale\tAnswith is encamped on the far side of a tower west of Brôntrig and south of Forthbrond. Ardwyn asked you to find the scout Answith and lend him your aid.\n",
[11405]="70028C9C\n1\tDestroy banners (total: 5)\tBanners can be found at the mouths of the mountain passes, south of Garrun's camp. Garrun has asked you to destroy the Dunlending banners posted along the mountain passes.\n2\tTalk to Garrun in the Isendale\tGarrun is at his camp, north of Cuvnerth and the mountain passes. You should report to Garrun and let him know that the banners have been removed.\n",
[11406]="7005B1F3\n1\tOrkish weapons can be found around Durshulot to the north-west, on the middle tier. Rékkur has asked you to destroy these weapons and sabotage the Orcs' periodic skirmishes with the Gabil'akkâ.\t\n2\tTalk to Rékkur in Aslíf\tYou have destroyed weapons around Durshulot. Rékkur in Aslíf will be glad to hear the news.\n",
[11407]="7002FEC8\n1\tDefeat goblin harriers (total: 6)\030Defeat Mordor siege-breakers (total: 3)\tFastred wants you to defeat riders on your journey to Walstow. Goblin and Orc riders can be found just off the road to the east.\n2\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig is in the mead-hall in Walstow.\n",
[11408]="70058573\n1\tTalk to Aighrig\tYou should discuss plans with Aighrig. She stands before the stairs to Annâk-khurfu.\n2\tDefeat bat-keepers at Tithzagáf (total: 4)\030Rescue infant bats (total: 5)\030Use the whistle to summon Aighrig to your side\tThe cave Tithzagáf is located on the island of Grytholm, to the north-west of Annâk-khurfu. You should defeat the bat-keepers there, as well as rescue infant bats from their influence.\n3\tUse the whistle to summon Aighrig to your side\030Deliver the infant bats to Aighrig\tYou and Aighrig have rescued several infant bats from the Angmarim. You should give the bats to Aighrig.\n",
[11409]="7000AC57\n1\tDeliver the kindling to Soldier Glat at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect Grimwood-kindling (total: 5)\tSearch the area of Hithlad for the kindling needed to make the arrow shafts. Hithlad and the Grimwood forest are south of Tol Ascarnen. In an effort to better fortify Tol Ascarnen, the War-tyrant has called to the goblins at Grothum and told his soldiers to craft bolts for the goblins to shoot into the tunnel at the mouth of the keep. It falls to you to collect the wood for the shafts.\n",
[11410]="7006B8EC\n1\tFind the Orc supplies in the northern part of Maurûsh\tFind the supplies the Orcs are using in the northern area of Maurûsh.\n2\tSabotage Orc supplies (total: 4)\tSabotage the Orc supplies you have found in the northern area of Maurûsh.\n3\tFind the Orc supplies in the western part of Maurush\tFind the supplies the Orcs are using in the western area of Maurûsh.\n4\tSabotage Orc supplies (total: 4)\tSabotage the Orc supplies you have found in the western area of Maurûsh.\n5\tSpeak to Galamka\tReturn to Galâmka in Ub Nishir and inform him of your success.\n",
[11411]="7000AC58\n1\tTalk to Soldier Kaasak at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect Drake-sinew (total: 5)\tThe Wintersebb-drakes are found north, in sections near the Hoarwell's source and at the foot of the Misty Mountains. Angmar's forces at Tol Ascarnen are crafting a great horn to call reinforcements to the fight when the Free Peoples return to assault the area. Kaasak has tasked you with collecting sinew from the Wintersebb-drakes to secure the many horns that will adorn the post.\n",
[11412]="7003FF25\n1\tDefeat Vandals (total: 6)\tThe Great Hall is the crown jewel of Dol Amroth.\n",
[11413]="70065F7B\n1\tPick up the box of pins\030Pick up the bundle of rope\tWharf master Annúngil has asked you to replace the damaged ropes and pins on the Rosigil. You should pick up the box of pins and bundles of new rope. The box of pins and the rope are next to Annúngil, on the docks in the Dol Amroth bay.\n2\tReplace stripped pins (total: 4)\030Replace frayed rope (total: 2)\tYou are now armed with fresh pins and tightly woven ropes. You should replace the pins on the Rosigil and the rope on the docks. The Rosigil is moored in the Dol Amroth bay.\n3\tReturn to Annúngil\tYou should let Annúngil know that you have replaced the damaged pins and piles of rope on the Rosigil. The wharf master is on a dock in the Dol Amroth bay.\n",
[11414]="70027320\n1\tFind Mostun and challenge him to combat\030Find Gaenor and challenge her to combat\tMostun and Gaenor are somewhere in the village of Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras. Mair wants you to challenge two masters of the fighting arts in Tûr Morva, so that they may learn from your fighting skills.\n2\tTalk to Mair in Tûr Morva\tMair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras. You have defeated both Mostun and Gaenor, and the pair have learned some of your fighting skills.\n",
[11415]="70067C48\n1\tMake your way to Grijâti, the Haradrim camp south-east of Jax Phanâl. Once there, find the ritual circle and plant the banner to draw out and challenge the strongest of the Haradrim warriors.\t\n2\tTalk to Stúkha\tYou defeated the Haradrim leader, and he said he would honour the pacts of the past. You should return to Stúkha at Jax Phanâl.\n",
[11416]="70015465\n1\tFind and talk to Krum\tKrum can be found to the north of the Chamber of the Cross-roads, near Ninknakh Faltor. Líkmund has asked you to speak with Krum regarding the goblin-camp he found and aid him as you may.\n2\tTalk to Líkmund at the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tLíkmund is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, south of Ninknakh Faltor. The camp at Ninknakh Faltor was indeed quite large and well-fortified, and you were only able to explore it in part. You should inform Líkmund of what you learned.\n",
[11417]="7004DA42\n1\tSpeak to Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth.\n",
[11418]="7004DB8C\n1\tSpeak to Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth.\n",
[11419]="7004DB8D\n1\tSpeak to Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth.\n",
[11420]="7004DA3F\n1\tTalk to Rock\tBy completing this quest, you will receive a Strongholds of the North barter currency allowance.\n",
[11421]="7004178A\n1\tFree slaves aboard the Corsair ships (total: 6)\tThe Corsair ships can be reached using the boat to the south of Thandor. You should board the Corsair ships and free the captured slaves.\n2\tTalk to Thandor\tThandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani. You should speak with Thandor.\n",
[11422]="70022419\n1\tFind the School of Tham Mírdain\tThe School of Tham Mírdain can be found in Mirobel, in the south-west region of Eregion. Gelriwen of Echad Mirobel has asked you to find the entrance to an ancient school.\n",
[11423]="70055008\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Student of the Enemy\n",
[11424]="7000ACA0\n1\tPresent your Studies of the Unknown to Cachúnir in Rivendell\030Craft Studies of the Unknown (total: 5)\tCachúnir is at Rivendell, in the Trollshaws. Cachúnir has asked you to pen some studies of the Unknown and bring them to him.\n",
})
